What is Headlamp?
    Headlamp is an open-source Kubernetes web UI developed by Kinvolk (now part of Microsoft).
    It lets you manage and monitor your Kubernetes cluster through a browser instead of relying only on kubectl commands.

Why do we need Headlamp?

Normally, to inspect Kubernetes resources, you run commands like:

kubectl get pods
kubectl describe pod logapp-abc123
kubectl logs logapp-abc123
kubectl get svc
kubectl get ingress
kubectl top pods

When managing many namespaces, deployments, and pods, this becomes tedious.

Headlamp provides a single UI to:

View cluster resources
Inspect pod logs
Check pod events
Scale deployments
View YAML manifests
Monitor workloads
Browse namespaces
Execute commands inside containers

